  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IBRD capital increase GCI SCI 2020-2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Norway is taking part in the 2018 General and Selective Capital of the International Bank for Reconstruction and Development (IBRD) with a paid-up share in Norwegian kroner (NOK) equivalent to a total USD 47 600 000, to be made in the period 2020-2023. This implies a subscription to 1390 (GCI) + 1938 (SCI) additional shares of the capital stock of the IBRD that were allocated under Resolutions No. 663 and 664 of the Board of Governors on October 1, 2018.</narrative>
  </description>
